# Copy to .env in this folder on the server, once. Owner root, mode 600, never in git.
# The guard keeps a second run from replacing a filled-in file:
#   [ -e .env ] || sudo install -m 600 -o root -g root .env.example .env
# Keep a copy of the filled-in file in the password manager.

# The secret the worker sends with every request to the app. The same value as
# STUDIO_WORKER_SECRET in ../app/.env, and no other secret's. Never typed: made on
# the server and written into both files, never shown (README.md, "S2"):
#   v=$(openssl rand -hex 24)
STUDIO_WORKER_SECRET=

# Where the app is: its proxy on the app stack's network. Change it only if the app's
# proxy is renamed.
STUDIO_APP_URL=http://ni-app-proxy:8080

# Deepgram's key, for the `transcribe` jobs (the fallback when the desktop app cannot
# transcribe on the person's own machine). The app's DEEPGRAM_API_KEY may be copied
# here. Empty: those jobs fail with a sentence saying so; everything else works.
DEEPGRAM_API_KEY=

# ElevenLabs' key, for narration in the Studio (the `voices` and `narration` jobs). Set,
# the editor offers "Rewrite voiceover" and the agent's narration tools work; empty,
# narration is off and nothing else changes. It is the workspace's own account: every
# paid request lands in the Studio's cost ledger, not in Native Intelligence's usage.
ELEVENLABS_API_KEY=
# (Generated shots need the higgsfield command-line tool installed and signed in where the
# worker runs. This image does not have it, so on the server they stay off; a worker on
# the owner's Mac, with the tool signed in, offers them.)
# (The motion check and the review need no setting here: the image's own python3 has numpy
# and OpenCV, and the worker finds it at start. STUDIO_ANALYSIS_PYTHON is for a worker run
# by hand: studio-worker/.env.example.)
# (Sound design needs earshot, an outside MIT-licensed tool at a reviewed commit, installed
# where the worker runs, named by STUDIO_EARSHOT_DIR (studio-worker/README.md, "Sound"). This
# image does not install it, so on the server sound design stays off and nothing else changes;
# a worker on the owner's Mac with earshot installed offers it. Once the image installs it
# (the commented lines in that README, "The image"), set STUDIO_EARSHOT_DIR=/opt/earshot here.)
STUDIO_EARSHOT_DIR=
# Whether renders run code scenes' code (graphics the agent wrote as React code, run in a locked
# frame with no network: studio-worker/README.md, "Code scenes"). Empty is OFF here (production):
# an export, stills or a check of a video with a code scene is then refused with a sentence. On
# this shared server the frame's only wall is Chrome's own sandbox, so `on` is the owner's call.
STUDIO_CODE_SCENES=

# Optional. Which job kinds this worker takes (comma separated; empty: all of import,
# export, stills, thumbnail, transcribe, slides, voices, narration, shot-quote, shot,
# continuity; the provider kinds only while their key or tool is there), jobs at once (1), Chrome tabs per
# render (2), and the asset cache's bound in bytes (5 GB).
STUDIO_WORKER_KINDS=
STUDIO_WORKER_CONCURRENCY=
STUDIO_RENDER_CONCURRENCY=
STUDIO_CACHE_BYTES=
